# Siblings the CI gate checks out (at their canonical origin head) next to this
# repo so the encoder's cross-repo byte-identity guards resolve them
# deterministically.
#
# xchain-hub: test/unit/coins-conformance.test.js compares src/coins against the
# canonical ../xchain-hub/src/coins.
#
# xchain-documentation: test/unit/ActionManifestConformance.test.js compares the
# vendored manifest against ../xchain-documentation/protocol/action-manifest.json.
#
# Both SKIP when the sibling is absent, which is right for a standalone deploy
# but is a trap on a shared CI venue that keeps a persistent checkout per repo:
# an undeclared sibling is then not absent at all, it is whatever revision
# another repo's run left behind, and the guard silently compares against that.
# Declaring them makes the harness ship canonical and remove any leftover.
xchain-hub
xchain-documentation
